Simple File Manager
Name Shikha Patel
Date Jan 2026, Last Modified Feb 2026

Overview:-
This project implements a simplified graphical file manager using wxWidgets. It supports:-
  Browsing directories (editable path bar)
  File listing with properties (name/type/size/last modified)
  Open (double-click or Enter)
  New folder, rename, delete
  Copy, cut, paste (virtual clipboard) with overwrite prompt
  Refresh and exit
  Keyboard shortcuts for all operations

Build:-
  make

Run:-
  ./filemanager

Notes:-
Requires wxWidgets (wx-config must be available).
Uses C++17 filesystem.
Single-selection list.
Copy/Cut/Paste uses a "virtual clipboard" (stores only one selected path and a mode).
The list may include ".." to navigate to the parent directory.
Double-click or Enter to open
Directory:- navigates into it
File:- opens with system default app

Controls / Shortcuts:-
  Enter/Double-click   Open selected item
  Ctrl+N                 New folder
  F2                     Rename
  Del                    Delete
  Ctrl+C                 Copy
  Ctrl+X                 Cut
  Ctrl+V                 Paste
  F5                     Refresh
  Ctrl+Q                 Exit

Attributions:-
Date/time conversion for std::filesystem timestamps may follow common cross-platform patterns.


Troubleshooting notes:
On minimal Linux/SSH environments, "Open" depends on system default applications. If no desktop apps are installed, you may see warnings or an error dialog; this still indicates the open attempt was made.
macOS (XQuartz/X11 forwarding): If the GUI opens but you see GLX/fbConfigs warnings, run: LIBGL_ALWAYS_INDIRECT=1 ./filemanager
